{{Quote|I am General Lok Durd of the Separatist Alliance. ''[&hellip;]'' You are now under the ''protection'' of the Separatist Alliance. I congratulate you on your good fortune.|Lok Durd to [[Tee Watt Kaa]]|audio=LokDurd1.flac|<ref name="Defenders of Peace" />}}
'''Lok Durd''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[Neimoidian]] arms developer who served as a [[general]] in the [[Separatist Droid Army]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Defenders of Peace" /> He was featured on the anti-[[Trade Federation]] poster ''[[Taxation Without Federation]]''.<ref name="Propaganda">''[[Star Wars Propaganda: A History of Persuasive Art in the Galaxy]]''</ref> He was [[Defense of Maridun|defeated]] by [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] forces and was taken into Republic [[Prison|custody]].<ref name="Defenders of Peace" /> Durd, along with [[Nuvo Vindi]], was part of [[Lieutenant Commander]] [[Orson Callan Krennic|Orson Krennic's]] original plans for a [[prisoner]] exchange with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] to secure the [[Vallt Rescue Operation|release]] of [[Galen Walton Erso|Galen Erso]], [[Lyra Erso]], and the baby [[Jyn Erso]] from imprisonment on [[Vallt]].<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref> However, Durd eventually managed to escape custody and went on to cause havoc beyond the [[Western Reaches]].<ref name="Rise">''[[Rise of the Separatists]]''</ref>

==Biography==
{{Quote|We test a new weapon, of my own design, which is capable of catastrophic destruction. A weapon which will destroy organic matter, but leave machines unharmed.|Lok Durd, on the defoliator|audio=LokDurd2.flac|<ref name="Defenders of Peace" />}}
[[File:LokDurddude2.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Lok Durd speaks with Count Dooku during the defoliator's first test.]]
Lok Durd was a corpulent [[Gender|male]] [[Neimoidian]] who operated as an arms developer of the monolithic [[Trade Federation]], eventually participating in the [[Clone Wars]] as a [[general]] in the [[Separatist Droid Army]]. A male [[Aqualish]], [[Pune Zignat]], accompanied Durd during the [[Defense of Maridun|battle]] on the [[planet]] [[Maridun]], where the Neimoidian wished to test the [[defoliator]] against a [[Lurmen village|colony]] of [[Lurmen]].<ref name="Defenders of Peace" /> Zignat was the real developer of the defoliator, but nonetheless, his superior claimed the design as his own creation.<ref name="HC 13">{{HelmetCollectionCite|13|Databank A-Z}}</ref> An ambitious [[Separatist officer]], General Durd's efforts strove to build a [[weapon]] worthy of both a promotion and the approval of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|CIS]]' [[Head of State]], [[Count of Serenno|Count]] [[Dooku]]. After running and making an inspection of the Lurmen village, the Neimoidian had the defoliator, which was equipped to a [[Defoliator Deployment Tank|DDT]], tested and contacted the [[Sith Lord]]. After informing [[Count]] Dooku of the weapon's capabilities against all organic matter and harmlessness towards their [[battle droid]]s, General Durd prepared to move his [[Lok Durd's battalion|battalion]] towards the settlement of [[Chief]] [[Tee Watt Kaa]]. His attempt at a definitive weapon testing proved unsuccessful as the combined efforts of [[Galactic Republic]] forces led by [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] and some of the Lurmen colonists prevented the destruction of the village, resulting in the capture of both the Neimoidian and his Aqualish assistant, Zignat.<ref name="Defenders of Peace" />

[[File:LokDurddude.png|thumb|right|250px|Lok Durd is captured by Skywalker.]]
As part of his plan to liberate the [[scientist]] [[Galen Walton Erso]] and his [[Erso family|family]] from [[Vallt]], [[Lieutenant Commander]] [[Orson Callan Krennic]] originally intended to exchange the still-captured General Durd and [[Doctor]] [[Nuvo Vindi]] for the valued prisoner held by the Confederacy. However, the Neimoidian ultimately escaped from Republic custody to rejoin his Separatist comrades,<ref name="Catalyst" /> causing chaos in the [[Western Reaches]] and, thus, forcing Krennic to make alterations to his initial designs.<ref name="Rise" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Personality and traits==
Lok Durd was a Neimoidian male weapons designer who served Count Dooku. The corpulent commander was 2.11 [[meter]]s (6 [[Foot|feet]], 11 inches) tall,<ref name="Join the Battle" /> and had [[Color|red]] [[eye]]s and gray skin. Durd served as a general in the Trade Federation, leading the Separatist Droid Army who landed on Maridun during the Clone Wars.<ref name="Defenders of Peace" /> He hoped his desires would bring him wealth and glory.<ref name="Join the Battle" /> Despite the success of the defoliator's test, Durd was captured by Anakin Skywalker and the Lurmen villagers. As a result, he whimpered that he would lose his promotion.<ref name="Defenders of Peace" />

==Skills and abilities==
Lok Durd was known for his exceptional weapons research, as well as his leadership skills and tactics.<ref name="Join the Battle" /> He was also proficient at the operation of [[Armored Assault Tank Mk I|AAT]]s.<ref name="Defenders of Peace" />

==Equipment==
Durd was armed with a pair of [[electrobinoculars]].<ref name="Defenders of Peace" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|We decided that going with this sort of really big, heavy, rolly guy with an even bigger hat than Nute Gunray's would just&hellip;would work, would sort of sell that this guy was extremely flamboyant and very bossy and even more gluttonous than your average Neimoidian.|Series Designer [[Kilian Plunkett]], on modeling Lok Durd|<ref name="The Complete Season One" />}}
Lok Durd first appeared in "[[Defenders of Peace]]" from [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|''The Clone Wars'' television series]]. He was voiced by [[George Takei]], and was intended as a recurring villain, though this never came to pass.<ref name="NA">{{WebCite|url=http://www.newsarama.com/tv/010919-George-Takei.html|text=From 'Trek' to 'Wars': George Takei on Clone Wars|work=Newsarama.com|date=2009-01-19|author=Steve Fritz|archivedate=20090121232020|nolive=1}}</ref> Concept art for the Neimoidian was created by [[Kilian Plunkett]].<ref name="Concept Art">{{WebCite|url=https://www.kilianplunkett.com/star-wars-the-clone-wars-galllery|text=Star Wars - The Clone Wars|work=[[Kilian Plunkett]]'s [https://www.kilianplunkett.com official website]|archivedate=20240524044437}}</ref> After seeing art of the character and reading the script, Takei understood he was going to play "a very pompous, full-of-himself bad guy."<ref name="Trek">{{SWArchive|url=fans/rocks/news20090123.html|text=George Takei: Trekking onto Clone Wars}}</ref>

